pnpm-lock.yaml

# Cross-repo contract — its bytes ARE the contract, so no formatter may rewrite them.
#
# This file must stay byte-identical with `rust-auth/conformance/wire-contract.json`; both
# libraries can back the same deployment, and each asserts its own implementation against its
# own copy. Nothing in either repo checks one copy against the other, so a reformat here breaks
# the pairing with no signal at all — and the `lint-staged` glob `*.{json,md,yml,yaml}` runs
# `prettier --write`, which means an ordinary commit was one formatting-default change away from
# doing exactly that.
#
# Do not remove this entry to make `format:check` "consistent". The file's canonical form is
# whatever both repos hold, not whatever Prettier would emit.
conformance/wire-contract.json
